course: dictionary
lesson: 10906
title: A visitor is someone who comes to stay a while
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A visitor is a person who comes to see a person or a place for a while, then goes home again. Visitors come to your house, to a museum, to a zoo, or to a city they do not live in. «A museum had 120 visitors on Monday and 95 on Tuesday.» Here visitor means one of the people who came through the door to look around.
explain: Look at the words around visitor to check its meaning. «Speak quietly in nature and leave music at home, because noise frightens animals and disturbs other visitors.» The words "other" and "disturbs" tell you the visitors are people who are in the same place, looking at the same thing as you.
explain: Visitor can also mean a person who looks at a website. «A visitor to a website» is someone who opens the page and reads it. The meaning is the same: someone who comes to look at something for a while, and does not live there.
fact: A visitor is a person who comes to see a person or a place for a while.
fact: Visitors to a place are often tourists, who come from another town or country.
fact: «Visitors must sign in» at a school office so staff know who is in the building.
fact: «A puppy jumps up at visitors» because it has learned that jumping gets attention.
fact: The word visitor comes from the word visit, which means to go and see someone or somewhere for a short time.
exercise: «A museum had 120 visitors on Monday and 95 on Tuesday.» What is a visitor? | A person who comes to see a place for a while | A room full of old paintings | *A person who works in the museum every day | A ticket for the museum
exercise: «Speak quietly in nature, because noise disturbs other visitors.» What does disturbs mean here? | Makes them laugh | Helps them to sleep | *Upsets or bothers | Brings them a present
exercise: «A long, hard stare can be a challenge in gorilla language, so keepers ask visitors not to stare at the gorillas.» Who are the visitors? | The gorillas themselves | The trees in the zoo | *People who come to see the gorillas | The keepers who look after them
test: Ella says a visitor is a person who lives next door. Is she right? | Yes, that is the same as a neighbour | Yes, visitors always live nearby | *No, a visitor does not live in that place | No, a visitor comes for a while and then goes home
test: «A bird that comes only in summer is a summer visitor.» What does visitor mean for this bird? | A bird that lives there all year | A bird that sings at night | A bird that cannot fly | *A bird that comes to a place for a while
exam: Jayden reads «Visitors must sign in at the school office and wear a badge.» Why must visitors do this? | So the visitors can have a free lunch | Because the badge is a prize | Because visitors are always late | *So staff know who is in the building
